results/
*.fastq.gz
*.fq.gz
*.bam
*.bai
*.vcf
*.vcf.gz
*.fasta
*.fa
*.fa.fai
dev/
out-dev/
.claude/

# The smoke dataset itself is 30 MB of simulated reads and a reference: it is
# a download, not source. Unzip it here; do not commit it.
smoke/

# Slurm writes one .out and one .err per array task into the directory you
# submitted from. They are run artefacts, not source; RESOURCES.md quotes the
# numbers that matter out of them.
slurm/logs/

# smoke-run/ is the exception the brief asks for: the two files from the full
# smoke run ARE submitted, and the rules above would otherwise swallow the VCF.
!smoke-run/
!smoke-run/**

# cluster-run/ is week 2's equivalent: the cohort job's filtered VCF and its
# manifest are submitted, and *.vcf.gz above would otherwise swallow the VCF
# silently - `git add -A` skips an ignored file without a word, which is how
# you discover at the deadline that the 20-mark deliverable was never committed.
!cluster-run/
!cluster-run/**
